      {
        "id": 82533,
        "name": "dpt",
        "username": "dpt",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/{size}/1922_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-12-13T11:05:25.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Oaktree\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/oaktree/48/2287_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Oaktree:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><b>Katsue wrote:</b></p>\n<div><blockquote>Get Out of the Way isn't great against Iron Legacy, unless you're in the Final Wasteland or something.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\n&nbsp;Yes. Confusing it with \"Know When To Turn Lose\".&nbsp; Need to verify card effects before I hit \"SAVE\".&nbsp; :p \n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>\"Know When to Turn Loose\" doesn't have the healing effect that \"Get Out of the Way\" does, so the Energy Forms would be superfluous. I think \"Know When to Turn Loose\" is too damaging for future development for anything but a finishing move, and Iron Legacy's Superhuman Redirection would probably prevent that from working.</p>",
