      {
        "id": 82534,
        "name": "Oaktree",
        "username": "Oaktree",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/oaktree/{size}/2287_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-12-13T16:15:49.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"dpt\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/48/1922_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> dpt:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>\"Know When to Turn Loose\" doesn't have the healing effect that \"Get Out of the Way\" does, so the Energy Forms would be superfluous. I think \"Know When to Turn Loose\" is too damaging for future development for anything but a finishing move, and Iron Legacy's Superhuman Redirection would probably prevent that from working.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>One thing I noticed from one of the Play-By-Forum battles against Iron Legacy was how effective Chrono Ranger was against him even with Superhuman Redirection in play.&nbsp; With a couple of bounties and the right one-shots he was just hitting for 3 HP repeatedly and not triggering Superhuman Redirection while still doing a considerable amount of accumulative damage in his turn.</p>",
